WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.290
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:15.290
The reading from the Sinaxadion for August 24, on which we commemorate the Holy Hyromarter

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:25.290
Cosmas Itolos equal to the Apostles and Evangelizer of Southern Albania, the memory of

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:33.130
the Holy New Hyromarter and equal to the Apostles, Cosmas of Itolia.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:40.410
Saint Cosmas was born in a small village in Itolia called Megadendron in the Diocese of Arta

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:48.330
in about the year 1714. His parents, simple and devout people, brought him up in the fear

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:56.370
of God and love of the Scriptures. At about the age of 20, he went to the Holy Mountain

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:02.890
of Athos to study at the Academy, which had been founded as a dependency of the monastery

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:10.890
of Vatopevi, where the famous Evgenios Bulgades was teaching. But the reactions provoked by the

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:17.050
founding of this establishment, which spread the spirit of the Enlightenment in the very

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:23.810
heart of the citadel of Orthodoxy, quickly forced Bulgades and other eminent professors

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:34.890
to leave Athos, and the Academy very soon fell into decline in the year 1759. This was for

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:42.490
the young Cosmas a sign of providence, and turning his back on his studies, he embraced the

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:50.570
monastic life in the monastery of Philothea, where his zeal for ascetic striving and his devotion

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:58.810
made him worthy to be ordained priest shortly after his monastic profession. The blessed man had,

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:06.170
from his youth, had a great desire to spread the word of God around him, to such a degree that he

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:13.210
said that the salvation of his brethren was devouring him as a grub eats away a tree from

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:20.410
the inside. In these difficult times for the oppressed Greek people, ignorance of the rudiments

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:27.610
of the faith and of Christian culture led to the neglect and decline of morals, so that the

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:35.210
preaching of the Gospel clearly became the most important task. But, warned by the teaching of

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:44.330
the fathers, Cosmas did not want to engage in apostolic life through his own will. Desiring to learn

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:52.090
if this was God's will, he randomly opened the holy scriptures one day, and his eyes lit on these

00:02:52.090 --> 00:03:02.970
words of the Apostle. Let no man seek his own, but every man another's. Thus enlightened by the

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:10.810
word of God, and after having taken counsel of the fathers of the Holy Mountain, he went to Constantinople

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:21.130
to receive the blessing of patriarch Seraphim II, in the years 1759 through 1761, and to take a few

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:28.810
lessons in rhetoric from his cousin, Archimandrite Kessantos, who was later to become the director of the

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:37.530
patriarchal academy, and then of the school of Naxos. The new Apostle began his preaching ministry

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:43.050
in the churches around Constantinople, and pushed on into the eastern parts of Greece,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:53.370
Nafbakti, Brakori, Mesolongion, and Thessaly, then returning to Constantinople. After having

00:03:53.450 --> 00:04:00.810
withdrawn to Athos for a time, he received authorization from patriarch Sofronios II, in the years

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:09.530
1774 through 1780, to go and preach in the Kikladis in order to console the people who had been

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:18.250
discouraged by the failure of an uprising, brought about by Russia in the year 1775. He returned

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:25.290
thens to make a retreat in the monasteries, thus completing 17 years of life on the Holy Mountain,

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:33.530
but his heart, burning with love for his brethren, would not allow him to stay there. He therefore

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:41.290
left for Thessalonica, stayed briefly in Berea, and traveled throughout Macedonia, gathering great

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:48.970
crowds of the faithful who listened to him with contrition. From Kefalonia he went to the island

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:58.410
of Sanquithos, and then on to Corfu, going thens to Appirus. There he found that Christianity was

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:06.250
an apparlous state, and he confirmed the Orthodox faith there, and put a stop to the people's conversion

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:15.770
to Islam. Helped by God's grace, St. Cosmos worked wonders in these regions, which have to this day

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:23.290
remained impregnated with echoes of his preaching. Through his exhortations he succeeded in restoring

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:30.810
a Christian way of life to the people. His words were simple, able to be understood by all,

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:38.250
using images and expressions taken from everyday life, but they were also full of gentleness,

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:46.410
peace, and joy that can only be the gift of the Holy Spirit. They had the virtue of penetrating

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:52.650
straight to the souls of his hearers, and of immediately being received with enthusiasm as the

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:59.290
expression of the will of God. As no church would have been able to contain the crowds that gathered

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:06.650
round the new apostle, he preached in the open air, standing on a portable platform beside a great

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:14.410
cross that had been stuck in the ground, and which, after he had left, became a source of healing

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:23.130
and consolation for both bodily and spiritual ills. He taught the Christians to live according to

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:31.210
Christ's commandments, and to observe Sunday, the Lord's day, setting aside their everyday work

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:41.450
to go to church and hear the Word of God. Wherever he went, he founded schools, a task that he considered

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:48.970
fundamental for the teaching of Greek and the Holy Scriptures. He persuaded the rich to devote their

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:56.730
surplus to almsgiving, and the distribution of devotional books, icons, and prayer ropes,

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:01.930
and also urged them to donate baptisteries to the churches for the baptism of children.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:10.250
A crowd of two or three thousand of the faithful followed him everywhere, becoming a veritable army

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:17.210
of Christ that traveled through the whole of Albania, following the saint, looking on him as

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:25.210
Enoch, or the prophet Elias, who had come to proclaim the dawn of a new age. Before beginning his

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:32.970
preaching, he would celebrate Vespers, or Aparatleses, a service of intercession to the mother of God.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:41.770
Then, after having spoken, he left it to fifty or so priests who accompanied him to continue his

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:49.210
work by the hearing of confessions, the celebrating of the office of Holy Unction, of Holy Communion,

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:55.770
and personal visits to each person. Although the saint's preaching had no polemical content,

00:07:56.410 --> 00:08:01.930
confirming itself to the teaching of the Evangelical Virtues, and also by virtue of his having

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:10.010
appeared before the Pasha of Yonina, and had received great honor from him. Certain Jews excited by

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:16.010
jealousy and furious ever since the saint had made them hold their Sunday markets on a Saturday,

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:26.090
persuaded the Pasha to put an end to his life. Cosmos had formed the habit of arriving in an area

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:31.690
in which he desired to preach, of going personally to ask the blessing of the local bishop,

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:37.770
and then sending one of his disciples to ask permission of the Turkish civil authorities,

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:46.410
arriving one day near the Albanian village of Kolikontasi. He learned that the Pasha of the region,

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:54.730
Kurt Pasha, lived not far away at Berati. Despite the urgings of those around him to prudence,

00:08:54.730 --> 00:09:00.650
the saint decided to go himself and seek authorization to preach from the local official,

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:07.530
who made it known to him that he had received orders, to hand him over to Kurt Pasha.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:17.130
On hearing these words, Saint Cosmos realized that the moment had come to crown his work

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:24.810
with martyrdom, and he gave thanks to Christ for having counted him worthy of such honor.

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:35.210
The next day, on the 24th of August in the year 1779, seven soldiers took him under escort

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:44.090
on the pretext of sending him to Kurt Pasha, but after two hours on the road, they stopped by the river

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:50.250
Pasha, and told him that he had already been sentenced to death by execution.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:10:00.890
The saint, filled with joy and thanksgiving to God, blessed the four corners of the universe

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:08.730
with a sign of the cross and prayed for the salvation of all Christians. He refused to have his

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:15.370
hands tied so that he could cross them, and it was without offering the least resistance

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:21.370
that he was hanged on a tree, and gloriously gave his soul into God's keeping.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.930
He was then 65 years old.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:33.370
The Christians who had rushed to gather the saint's body, thrown into the river by his executioners,

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:41.930
into their nets, were left empty-handed, but a priest called Mark, being armed with prayer,

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:49.690
discovered the precious relics three days later, floating upright on the waves, as though the saint

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:56.730
were still alive. He was taken out of the water and, after being clad in his monastic habit,

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:04.650
was given worthy burial. A great many miracles were wrought at his tomb through the intervention of

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:15.050
his relics. In the year 1813, Ali Pasha of Ionina, whose glorious future Saint Kosmas had predicted,

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:24.010
had a church and monastery built at his tomb, and he gave his skull in a silver reliquary to his

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:32.890
Christian wife Basilica. Saint Kosmas, whose preaching had contributed in a decisive way to the

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:40.170
awakening of faith and national feeling among the Greeks, was immediately venerated by the people

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:49.930
as a new apostle and a prince among the new martyrs. But his veneration was only officially recognized

00:11:50.010 --> 00:12:00.090
by the Patriarchate of Constantinople in the year 1961. Through the prayers of our holy fathers,

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:11.610
O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
